      "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago",
      "rating": 1,
      "text": {
        "text": "I've noticed Google Ratings has started incorporating AI-powered photo analysis.\n\nPreviously, after uploading a photo, I had to write a caption. Now, Google directly \"tells a story from the picture,\" displaying related text descriptions (such as dish names, restaurant atmosphere, type of food, etc.), and the accuracy is quite high.\n\nWhile I'm experiencing the convenience of AI assisting my life, this sudden redesign was still a bit of a shock. How did it change so quietly? Shouldn't they have asked users first how much AI they want permeating their lives?\n\nConvenience is certainly great, but I don't want to unknowingly become accustomed to and dependent on AI, thereby losing my original ability to express my thoughts through writing.",
        "languageCode": "en"
      },
