      "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago",
      "rating": 1,
      "text": {
        "text": "This review is for a warranty request from Google for my wife’s Fitbit Charge 6.\n\nI was on a chat with Google this evening for 38 minutes trying to see about getting warranty service on her Fitbit that quit charging.\n\nAfter going through all the recommendations again, as I tried all the tips prior to starting the chat, I was asked to provide a copy of the receipt.\n\nThis is when I was told that her Fitbit was not covered by the manufacturer warranty because it wasn’t purchased through an authorized dealer.\n\nReally, here’s my beef. It was purchased on Amazon just like most everything else I buy online.\n\nI feel like this is a bullshit way to avoid providing a warranty on your product.\n\nI wonder how many folks have purchased a Fitbit on Amazon and not be aware that they have no warranty.\n\nAll three of our family members wear a Fitbit. Been wearing them for years.\n\nI won’t buy another Fitbit now that I know their policy.",
        "languageCode": "en"
      },
